-the-pacific-northwest-and-they-look-like-they-came-straight-out-of-a-horror-movie-180989598/</guid></item><item><title>涉嫌“毫无意义的破坏行为”摧毁了新安装的本杰明·哈里森雕像后，纵火调查正在进行中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-arson-investigation-is-underway-after-a-suspected-sensless-act-of-vandalism-destroys-a-newly-installed-benjamin-harrison-statue-180989605/</link><description>这件 3D 打印作品由印第安纳大学印第安纳波利斯分校的学生和教师制作，并于 9 月 16 日安装</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:33:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-arson-investigation-is-underway-after-a-suspected-sensless-act-of-vandalism-destroys-a-newly-installed-benjamin-harrison-statue-180989605/</guid></item><item><title>新展览聚焦 4,500 年来破碎、爆炸和退化的艺术品，探索“碎片的力量”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-spotlights-4500-years-of-broken-shot-up-and-degraded-artworks-to-explore-the-power-of-the-fragment-180989602/</link><description>该展览将在佛罗伦萨展出，并于明年在华盛顿举行，探讨了不同时期和不同文化中被毁坏雕塑的历史和影响</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-spotlights-4500-years-of-broken-shot-up-and-degraded-artworks-to-explore-the-power-of-the-fragment-180989602/</guid></item><item><title>观看 2026 年尼康喜剧野生动物奖入围照片和视频中捕捉到的搞笑动物恶作剧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-hilarious-animal-shenanigans-captured-in-photos-and-videos-shortlisted-for-the-2026-nikon-comedy-wildlife-awards-180989600/</link><description>从打喷嚏的驼鹿到现实生活中的愤怒的小鸟，今年的比赛收到了来自 112 个国家/地区的 10,000 多份参赛作品</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 23:01:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-hilarious-animal-shenanigans-captured-in-photos-and-videos-shortlisted-for-the-2026-nikon-comedy-wildlife-awards-180989600/</guid></item><item><title>阔别 12 年后，亚历山大·考尔德最后一座猛犸象雕塑终于完整回归国会山</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-a-12-year-absence-alexander-calders-mammoth-last-sculpture-finally-returns-in-full-to-capitol-hill-180989601/</link><description>考尔德的最后一部作品《山与云》因担心其结构完整性而于 2014 年被从哈特参议院办公大楼拆除</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 16:44:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/after-a-12-year-absence-alexander-calders-mammoth-last-sculpture-finally-returns-in-full-to-capitol-hill-180989601/</guid></item><item><title>四头白鲸从加拿大废弃的海洋公园获救几周后死亡。动物是否病得太重而无法移动？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/four-beluga-whales-died-weeks-after-being-rescued-from-a-defunct-marine-park-in-canada-were-the-animals-too-sick-to-be-moved-180989597/</link><description>他们是今年夏天从该设施转移的 30 头鲸鱼之一。在 2024 年关闭之前，它曾面临多项忽视和虐待动物的指控</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 15:34:19 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/four-beluga-whales-died-weeks-after-being-rescued-from-a-defunct-marine-park-in-canada-were-the-animals-too-sick-to-be-moved-180989597/</guid></item><item><title>挪威快速融化的山冰中出现了一个令人兴奋但“残酷”的发现，一支有 5000 年历史的箭</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-an-exciting-but-brutal-find-a-5000-year-old-arrow-emerges-from-norways-rapidly-melting-mountain-ice-180989599/</link><description>考古学家最近在尤通黑门山进行为期三周的探险，发现了 48 支史前箭</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 14:39:13 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-an-exciting-but-brutal-find-a-5000-year-old-arrow-emerges-from-norways-rapidly-melting-mountain-ice-180989599/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下今年的胖熊周冠军：背包，一位悠闲的 20 岁男性，“河上坚忍的存在”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-this-years-chonky-champion-of-fat-bear-week-backpack-a-laid-back-20-year-old-male-whos-a-stoic-presence-on-the-river-180989595/</link><description>这只棕熊因吃鲑鱼而发胖，现在体重在 1,000 至 1,200 磅之间，因此在幼崽时获得了绰号。当他小的时候，他喜欢骑在妈妈的背上，看她游过河</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-this-years-chonky-champion-of-fat-bear-week-backpack-a-laid-back-20-year-old-male-whos-a-stoic-presence-on-the-river-180989595/</guid></item><item><title>第一个女法老？研究人员称，一张古代象形文字的旧照片凸显了埃及最早的女王之一的地位</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-first-female-pharaoh-an-old-photo-of-ancient-hieroglyphics-highlights-the-status-of-one-of-egypts-earliest-queens-researchers-say-180989594/</link><description>一件失落已久的文物的黑白照片描绘了四个塞拉克，这是埃及统治者的象征，最近的一项研究表明，其中两个是她的</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-first-female-pharaoh-an-old-photo-of-ancient-hieroglyphics-highlights-the-status-of-one-of-egypts-earliest-queens-researchers-say-180989594/</guid></item><item><title>SpaceX 的巨型星舰火箭首次尝试抵达地球轨道，但发动机问题迫使其提前返回地球</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacexs-giant-starship-rocket-reached-earth-orbit-on-its-first-try-but-engine-problems-forced-it-to-return-to-the-planet-early-180989596/</link><description>两家航空航天公司正在竞相制造美国宇航局在将人类送回月球表面时使用的月球着陆器。但要到达我们的月球伙伴，航天器首先必须进入地球轨道</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:30:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacexs-giant-starship-rocket-reached-earth-orbit-on-its-first-try-but-engine-problems-forced-it-to-return-to-the-planet-early-180989596/</guid></item><item><title>一幅神秘的粉笔画在意大利私人收藏中被重新发现，被确认为爱德华·马奈失传已久的作品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-enigmatic-chalk-drawing-rediscovered-in-a-private-italian-collection-has-been-identified-as-the-long-lost-work-of-edouard-manet-180989593/</link><description>一个年轻女孩的素描，采用了马奈 1860 年代生活研究的红色粉笔特征，被认为与该艺术家的几幅画有关</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:55:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-enigmatic-chalk-drawing-rediscovered-in-a-private-italian-collection-has-been-identified-as-the-long-lost-work-of-edouard-manet-180989593/</guid></item><item><title>土星的卫星土卫二可能存在外星生命吗？地球微生物可以在其模拟环境中生存，提高其潜在的宜居性</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-saturns-moon-enceladus-host-alien-life-earth-microbes-can-live-in-its-simulated-environment-boosting-its-potential-habitability-180989589/</link><description>土卫二被冰覆盖，但该层可能隐藏着地下海洋。研究人员长期以来一直想知道咸水体是否具有适宜生命生存的条件，现在，一个研究小组表明，地球上喜热的生物体可以在那里繁衍生息</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:00:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-saturns-moon-enceladus-host-alien-life-earth-microbes-can-live-in-its-simulated-environment-boosting-its-potential-habitability-180989589/</guid></item><item><title>东北复活节期间，有人发现一只鲨鱼在新泽西州被洪水淹没的街道上游动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</link><description>该生物已被确认为光滑角鲨，这是一种在西大西洋发现的无害物种。它并不是唯一陷入风暴系统带来的混乱的动物</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-shark-was-spotted-swimming-through-the-flooded-streets-of-new-jersey-during-the-noreaster-180989588/</guid></item><item><title>英格兰备受喜爱的梧桐树在被破坏者砍倒三年后又显露出生命迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</link><description>现在，位于英格兰北部哈德良长城附近的树桩底部周围正在长出许多绿叶芽。</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/englands-beloved-sycamore-gap-tree-is-showing-signs-of-life-three-years-after-vandals-chopped-it-down-180989591/</guid></item><item><title>当简·奥斯汀在巴斯的舞厅转一圈时，古罗马文物就藏在她的脚下。现在，考古学家终于找到了它们</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</link><description>最近在英格兰巴斯集会室进行的发掘发现了罗马时代的硬币、屋顶瓦片、陶器、玻璃器皿、沟渠网络和军用头盔的碎片</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-jane-austen-took-a-turn-about-the-ballroom-in-bath-ancient-roman-artifacts-were-hiding-beneath-her-feet-now-archaeologists-have-finally-found-them-180989592/</guid></item><item><title>核磁共振扫描可能会在大脑中出现蛛丝马迹七年前发现阿尔茨海默病的迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</link><description>并非所有研究人员都相信通过 MRI 检测到的大脑变化足以成为诊断工具。但这些发现可以帮助研究人员更好地了解驱动神经退行性疾病的机制</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:33:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mri-scans-might-reveal-signs-of-alzheimers-disease-seven-years-before-a-telltale-marker-appears-in-the-brain-180989570/</guid></item><item><title>在罗马最著名和最被忽视的别墅之一，由修女绘制的具有数百年历史的下流壁画重新出现</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</link><description>耗资 4000 万美元修复西尔维斯特里里瓦尔迪别墅近一年后，保护人员正在重新发现和复兴 16 世纪的艺术</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-one-of-romes-most-famed-and-neglected-villas-centuries-old-risque-frescoes-painted-over-by-nuns-have-reappeared-180989585/</guid></item><item><title>Anthropic 表示其人工智能发现了一种新的酶系统，类似于革命性的基因编辑工具 CRISPR</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</link><description>该公司的专家不知道新发现的系统有什么作用，因此它在生物学中的潜在用途（如果有的话）仍不清楚。但这项工作标志着一项重大进步，因为人工智能主要是靠自己做出这一发现的</description><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/anthropic-says-its-ai-discovered-a-new-enzyme-system-that-resembles-the-revolutionary-gene-editing-tool-crispr-180989578/</guid></item></channel></rss>